<figure class="commit" data-r45-commit aria-labelledby="r45-title">
 <figcaption id="r45-title"><span>Figure 1</span> STAGING is only part of the commit condition</figcaption>
 <label>Final write acknowledgements <select data-case><option value="all">All required writes confirmed</option><option value="waiting">One required write unconfirmed</option></select></label>
 <div class="scene"><p class="identity">One purchase · one transaction identity</p><div class="participants"><section><p class="panel-title">Stock keys</p><p data-stock data-live>P3 12 · P7 1</p></section><section><p class="panel-title">Order and line keys</p><p data-order data-live>No 103</p></section><section><p class="panel-title">Transaction record</p><p data-record data-live>Not yet needed</p></section></div><p class="decision" data-decision data-live>Purchase not committed</p><p data-caller data-live>Caller has no commit success</p></div>
 <p data-explanation data-live aria-live="polite">Rewind before 103. Stock is unchanged and the purchase has not been written.</p>
 <div class="playback"><button data-play type="button">Play</button><button data-back type="button">Back</button><button data-next type="button">Next</button><span data-step></span><button data-reset type="button">Reset</button></div><div data-hold aria-hidden="true"><span></span></div>
 <details><summary>Read the commit condition as text</summary><p>Writes begin as intents. A STAGING record identifies required in-flight writes. STAGING plus proof that all required writes succeeded establishes implicit commit. Later COMMITTED and intent resolution make that decision cheaper to read. STAGING alone, or one unconfirmed write, is insufficient evidence for success.</p></details>
 <p class="caption">A Parallel Commits model, with logical groups of keys rather than observed range placement. Each relevant write must satisfy its range’s replication protocol. The drawing omits fast paths, individual messages and elapsed time; an unconfirmed write is not proved absent or aborted.</p>
</figure>
<script>
 import {stepper} from '../../figures/stepper.mjs';
 const root=document.querySelector('[data-r45-commit]');
 if(root){const choice=root.querySelector('[data-case]') as HTMLSelectElement;
 const player=stepper(root,{steps:()=>5,draw:(step)=>{const all=choice.value==='all',committed=all&&step>=3,clean=all&&step===4;
 root.querySelector('[data-stock]').textContent=step===0?'P3 12 · P7 1':clean?'P3 10 · P7 0 · resolved values':'P3 10 · P7 0 · provisional intents';
 root.querySelector('[data-order]').textContent=step===0?'No 103':clean?'103 and two lines · resolved values':'103 and two lines · provisional intents';
 root.querySelector('[data-record]').textContent=step===0?'Not yet needed':step===1?'PENDING / coordinator bookkeeping':clean?'COMMITTED, then safe cleanup':'STAGING + required write list';
 root.querySelector('[data-decision]').textContent=committed?'Purchase committed':step>=3?'Outcome not yet proved by these acknowledgements':'Purchase not yet committed';
 root.querySelector('[data-caller]').textContent=committed?'Coordinator may return commit success':'Caller has no commit success';
 root.querySelector('[data-explanation]').textContent=[
 'Rewind before 103. Stock is unchanged and the purchase has not been written.',
 'The transaction creates provisional writes under one identity. Ordinary readers cannot treat an individual intent as a committed purchase.',
 'The coordinator stages the transaction record while final writes can still be in flight. Seeing STAGING alone does not establish commit.',
 all?'All required writes are confirmed. Together with STAGING, this establishes implicit commit, before final intent cleanup.':'One required write is unconfirmed. The coordinator cannot infer success from the other writes; a missing acknowledgement does not itself prove abort.',
 all?'Cleanup makes the commit explicit and resolves intents. It changes the representation of the known outcome, rather than creating a second purchase.':'This chosen history has no further evidence. Recovery must resolve the transaction under the engine’s protocol; the client cannot declare either outcome from this picture.'
 ][step];}});choice.addEventListener('change',()=>player.render());}
</script>
<style>
.commit{margin:2.5rem 0;font-family:var(--font-sans)}figcaption{font:1.25rem/1.4 var(--font-serif);margin-bottom:.8rem}figcaption>span{font:.75rem var(--font-sans);text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--color-text-secondary);margin-right:.5rem}label{display:grid;gap:.4rem;font:.85rem/1.5 var(--font-sans);padding:.8rem;background:var(--color-surface-alt)}select,button{font:inherit;color:var(--color-text);background:var(--color-surface);border:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary);padding:.55rem}.scene{padding:1rem;border:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary)}.identity{font:.85rem/1.5 var(--font-sans);border-bottom:1px dashed var(--color-text-secondary);padding-bottom:.8rem}.participants{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.7rem}.participants section{margin:0;border:1px solid var(--color-accent);padding:.8rem}.participants .panel-title{min-height:0;font:600 .9rem/1.4 var(--font-sans);margin:0}.participants p{font:.85rem/1.55 var(--font-sans);margin:.7rem 0 0;min-height:5em}.decision{font:600 1rem/1.5 var(--font-sans);border:2px solid var(--color-accent);padding:.7rem}[data-caller]{font:.85rem/1.5 var(--font-sans)}[data-explanation]{font:.9rem/1.55 var(--font-sans);border-left:3px solid var(--color-accent);padding:.6rem .8rem;min-height:5em}.playback{display:flex;gap:.5rem;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap;padding:.8rem;background:var(--color-surface-alt)}button{cursor:pointer}[aria-disabled=true]{opacity:.55}[data-hold]{height:3px;background:var(--color-surface-alt)}[data-hold] span{display:block;height:3px;width:0;background:var(--color-accent)}details,.caption{font:.8rem/1.5 var(--font-sans);margin-top:1rem}.caption{color:var(--color-text-secondary)}@media(max-width:550px){.participants{grid-template-columns:1fr}.participants p{min-height:0}.decision{font-size:.9rem}}
</style>
